"None\nYou are correct that in C++11 and later, the initialization of a const array member with another array reference is not allowed. This is because C++11 introduced the rule of five (or the rule of three, depending on whether you're using old C++11), which states that if you have a class with at least five member functions, and one of them is a copy constructor, move constructor, copy assignment operator, move assignment operator, or destructor, then you must provide an implementation for all of them.\n\nIn your case, you have a class `flat_map` with a private member `elements` which is an array of pairs. The array initialization requires a brace-enclosed initializer list, which is not allowed for a const array member. Therefore, you cannot initialize the `elements` array with another array reference in the constructor.\n\nIf you want to use a const array member, you should remove the initialization in the constructor or make it non-const. Here's how you can modify your code:\n\n```cpp\nclass flat_map\n{\nprivate:\n    struct pair\n    {\n        key_type key;\n        value_type value;\n    };\n    const pair elements[N];\n\npublic:\n    flat_map() // remove initialization\n        : elements(0) // initialize with 0 elements\n\n    [[nodiscard]] consteval value_type operator[](const key_type key) const\n    {\n        for (const pair &elem : elements)\n            if (elem.key == key)\n                return elem.value;\n        throw &quot;Key not found&quot;;\n    }\n};\n```\n\nAlternatively, you can also make the `elements` array non-const:\n\n```cpp\nclass flat_map\n{\nprivate:\n    struct pair\n    {\n        key_type key;\n        value_type value;\n    };\n    const pair& elements[N]; // make it non-const\n\npublic:\n    flat_map() // remove initialization\n        : elements(nullptr) // initialize with nullptr\n\n    [[nodiscard]] consteval value_type operator[](const key_type key) const\n    {\n        for (const pair &elem : elements)\n            if (elem.key == key)\n                return elem.value;\n        throw &quot;Key not found&quot;;\n    }\n};\n```"
