"```python\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport pathlib\n\n# Define the path to the ultralytics library\nULTRALYTICS_PATH = pathlib.Path.home() / \".local\" / \"share\" / \"ultralytics\" / \"pytorch\"\n\n# Define the path to the CUDA library (if not installed)\nCUDA_PATH = pathlib.Path.home() / \".local\" / \"share\" / \"cudnn\"\nif not CUDA_PATH.exists():\n    CUDA_PATH = None\n\ndef get_libcublas_path():\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the path to the libcublas library.\n    \"\"\"\n    # If the library is installed, return the path\n    if CUDA_PATH is not None:\n        return ULTRALYTICS_PATH / \"libcublas.so\"\n    else:\n        # If the library is not installed, try to find it in the system path\n        for path in sys.path:\n            libcublas_path = path / \"libcublas.so\"\n            if libcublas_path.exists():\n                return libcublas_path\n        # If the library is not found in the system path, raise an error\n        raise ValueError(\"libcublas.so not found in the system path\")\n\ndef get_cudnn_path():\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the path to the cudnn library.\n    \"\"\"\n    # If the library is installed, return the path\n    if CUDA_PATH is not None:\n        return CUDA_PATH / \"cudnn-9.0\"\n    else:\n        # If the library is not installed, try to find it in the system path\n        for path in sys.path:\n            cudnn_path = path / \"cudnn-9.0\"\n            if cudnn_path.exists():\n                return cudnn_path\n        # If the library is not found in the system path, raise an error\n        raise ValueError(\"cudnn-9.0 not found in the system path\")\n\ndef configure_django():\n    \"\"\"\n    Configures the Django project to use the ultralytics library.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Add the ultralytics library to the INSTALLED_APPS setting\n    # in the settings.py file\n    os.environ[\"INSTALLED_APPS\"] = [\n        # ... other installed apps ...\n        \"ultralytics\",\n        # ... other installed apps ...\n    ]\n    # Add the ultralytics library to the MIDDLEWARE setting\n    # in the settings.py file\n    os.environ[\"MIDDLEWARE\"] = [\n        # ... other middleware ...\n        \"ultralytics\",\n        # ... other middleware ...\n    ]\n    # Add the ultralytics library to the CACHES setting\n    # in the settings.py file\n    os.environ[\"CACHES\"] = {\n        # ... other cache settings ...\n        \"ultralytics\",\n        # ... other cache settings ...\n    }\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"\n    Main function to configure the ultralytics library.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Get the libcublas path\n    libcublas_path = get_libcublas_path()\n    # Get the cudnn path\n    cudnn_path = get_cudnn_path()\n    # If the libcublas path is not found, raise an error\n    if libcublas_path is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"libcublas.so not found in the system path\")\n    # If the cudnn path is not found, raise an error\n    if cudnn_path is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"cudnn-9.0 not found in the system path\")\n    # Configure the Django project\n    configure_django()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```"
"None\nYou are experiencing the same issue of getting a `TemplateDoesNotExist` error when using Crispy Forms in Django. This issue is not specific to a particular template or form, but rather a general problem with how Crispy Forms is handling the template loaders.\n\nThe `TemplateDoesNotExist` error is raised because Crispy Forms is unable to find a template with the specified name in the correct directory. In your case, it seems that the templates are not being installed correctly.\n\nTo fix this issue, you need to make sure that the templates are installed correctly. You can try the following steps:\n\n1. Check the `settings.py` file to ensure that the `CRISPY_TEMPLATE_PACK` is set to a valid directory.\n\n```\nCRISPY_TEMPLATE_PACK = 'bootstrap4'\n```\n\n2. Make sure that the templates are installed in the correct directory. You can check the directory structure of your project by running the following command in your terminal:\n\n```bash\npython manage.py shell\nfrom django.conf import settings\nprint(settings.TEMPLATES[0].DIRS[0])\n```\n\n3. If the templates are not installed in the correct directory, you can try installing them manually using pip:\n\n```\npip install django-bootstrap4\n```\n\n4. After installing the templates, try running your Django application again. If the issue persists, it may be worth trying a different Crispy Forms version or installing it using a different method (e.g. via pip).\n\nAdditionally, you can try to debug the issue by checking the following:\n\n* Make sure that the `crispy_forms` package is installed correctly by running `pip show crispy-forms` in your terminal.\n* Check the Django documentation for Crispy Forms to ensure that you are using it correctly.\n* Try creating a new template and see if it works. If it does, then the issue is likely with your current template."
