"```java\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;\nimport java.util.concurrent.Executors;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor;\n\npublic class FindMultiples {\n\n    public static ArrayList<Integer> dividends = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    public static int getSum(int n) {\n        int sum = 0;\n        ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(3);\n        executor.submit(() -> {\n            for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n                if (i % 3 == 0 || i % 5 == 0 || i % 7 == 0) {\n                    temp = i;\n                    dividends.add(temp);\n                }\n            }\n        });\n        executor.shutdown();\n\n        Set<Integer> set = new HashSet<>(dividends);\n        dividends.clear();\n        dividends.addAll(set);\n\n        for (int i : dividends) {\n            sum += i;\n        }\n\n        return sum;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        System.out.println(getSum(1000));\n        System.out.println(getSum(76293));\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe problem with your code is that you are reusing the `set` to store unique integers, which is not necessary. Instead, you should use a `HashSet` to store unique integers. Additionally, you should remove the `temp` variable as it is not necessary. The `increment` method is also not necessary as you can directly add the number to the `dividends` list. \n\nThe `getSum` method uses a fixed thread pool of 3 threads to find the numbers that are divisible by 3, 5, or 7. However, this approach has a problem. The numbers are being added to the `dividends` list in the wrong order. The numbers that are divisible by 3 should be added first, then the numbers that are divisible by 5, and finally the numbers that are divisible by 7. \n\nTo fix this issue, you can modify the `getSum` method to add the numbers to the `dividends` list in the correct order. \n\nHere's the corrected code:\n\n```java\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;\nimport java.util.concurrent.Executors;\nimport java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor;\n\npublic class FindMultiples {\n\n    public static ArrayList<Integer> dividends = new ArrayList<>();\n\n    public static int getSum(int n) {\n        int sum = 0;\n        ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(3);\n        executor.submit(() -> {\n            for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n                if (i % 3 == 0 || i % 5 == 0 || i % 7 == 0) {\n                    dividends.add(i);\n                }\n            }\n        });\n        executor.shutdown();\n\n        Set<Integer> set = new HashSet<>(dividends);\n        dividends.clear();\n        dividends.addAll(set);\n\n        for (int i : dividends) {\n            sum += i;\n        }\n\n        return sum;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        System.out.println(getSum(1000));\n        System.out.println(getSum(76293));\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis corrected code will produce the correct result for the given input."
