"To find a parallel 2D lattice in a 3D lattice that best matches a given reference 2D lattice, you can use a topology-matching algorithm. Here's a step-by-step approach:\n\n1. Calculate the reciprocal lattice vectors of the reference 2D lattice.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the reciprocal lattice vectors of the reference 2D lattice\nref_rec_lattice_vectors = np.array([[2.5178270133578393, 0.0, 0.0],\n                                    [0.0, 2.5178270133578393, 0.0],\n                                    [0.0, 0.0, 5.341117665]])\n```\n\n2. Calculate the reciprocal lattice vectors of the 3D lattice.\n\n```python\n# Define the unit cell vectors of the 3D lattice\nbulk_unit_cell_vectors = np.array([[5.44370237, 0.0, 0.0],\n                                     [0.0, 5.44370237, 0.0],\n                                     [0.0, 0.0, 5.44370237]])\n\n# Calculate the reciprocal lattice vectors of the 3D lattice\nrec_lattice_vectors = np.dot(bulk_unit_cell_vectors, ref_rec_lattice_vectors.T)\n```\n\n3. Calculate the lattice vectors of the best-matched 2D lattice unit cell.\n\n```python\n# Define the unit cell vectors of the reference 2D lattice\nref_unit_cell_vectors = np.array([[3.8492788605882797, 0.0, 0.0],\n                                  [0.0, 3.8492788605882797, 0.0],\n                                  [0.0, 0.0, 8.165553555]])\n\n# Calculate the lattice vectors of the best-matched 2D lattice unit cell\nbest_match_lattice_vectors = np.dot(ref_unit_cell_vectors, ref_rec_lattice_vectors.T)\n```\n\n4. Calculate the fractional coordinates of the best-matched 2D lattice unit cell.\n\n```python\n# Calculate the fractional coordinates of the best-matched 2D lattice unit cell\nfractional_coords = best_match_lattice_vectors / np.linalg.norm(best_match_lattice_vectors)\n```\n\n5. Calculate the Cartesian coordinates of the best-matched 2D lattice unit cell.\n\n```python\n# Calculate the Cartesian coordinates of the best-matched 2D lattice unit cell\ncartesian_coords = fractional_coords * np.linalg.norm(best_match_lattice_vectors)\n```\n\n6. Calculate the MAE/RMSE between the fractional coordinates of the two cells.\n\n```python\n# Calculate the MAE/RMSE between the fractional coordinates of the two cells\nmae_rmse = np.sqrt(np.mean((cartesian_coords - np.array(ref_coords)) ** 2))\n```\n\n7. Return the best-matched 2D lattice unit cell.\n\n```python\nreturn best_match_lattice_vectors, cartesian_coords, mae_rmse\n```"
