"```python\nimport SwiftUI\n\nstruct PreviewItem: Identifiable {\n    let id = UUID()\n    var previewImage: String\n}\n\nclass PreviewItemManager {\n    var items: [PreviewItem] = []\n    \n    func addItem(item: PreviewItem) {\n        items.append(item)\n    }\n    \n    func removeItem(at index: Int) {\n        items.remove(at: index)\n    }\n    \n    func previewItem(at offset: Offset, in view: AnyView) -> AnyView {\n        return AnyView(\n            ZStack(alignment: .center) {\n                view\n                HStack {\n                    Spacer()\n                    Image(systemName: \"pencil\")\n                        .font(.system(size: 24))\n                        .foregroundColor(.gray)\n                    Spacer()\n                }\n                .padding(.horizontal, 16)\n                .padding(.vertical, 8)\n                .background(Color.white)\n                .cornerRadius(8)\n            }\n        )\n    }\n}\n\nstruct PreviewItemView: View {\n    @StateObject var previewItemManager = PreviewItemManager()\n    @State private var previewItem: PreviewItem? = nil\n    \n    var body: some View {\n        NavigationView {\n            List {\n                ForEach(previewItemManager.items) { item in\n                    Button(action: {\n                        previewItemManager.addItem(item: item)\n                    }) {\n                        previewItemManager.previewItem(at: .zero, in: self)\n                    }\n                    .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, maxHeight: .infinity)\n                    .background(Color.white)\n                    .cornerRadius(8)\n                    .padding(.horizontal, 16)\n                    .padding(.vertical, 8)\n                    .foregroundColor(.blue)\n                }\n            }\n            .navigationBarTitle(\"Preview\")\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nstruct PreviewItemView_Previews: PreviewProvider {\n    static var previews: some View {\n        PreviewItemView()\n    }\n}\n```"
"None\n\nImage::Magick is gone from Perl CPAN due to a decision by the Perl developers to discontinue its maintenance. The module was last actively maintained in 2019, and since then, it has not been updated or released new versions.\n\nTo install ImageMagick, you can use a package manager like CPAN (if you still have it installed) or a third-party package manager like Homebrew on macOS, or apt-get on Ubuntu-based distributions. Alternatively, you can use the `py imagemagick` library, which provides a Python interface to ImageMagick, although it is not as powerful as the original module.\n\nIf you are looking for alternative image processing libraries in Python, you may want to consider using OpenCV, Pillow (PIL), or other libraries that offer similar functionality."
"None\nYou are using the `CollectionView` with `RemainingItemsThreshold` set to `5`. This means that the collection view will only display the last 5 items in the data source. If you want to display all items, you should set `RemainingItemsThreshold` to `null` or remove the `RemainingItemsThresholdReachedCommand` binding.\n\nHere's how you can modify your XAML to achieve this:\n\n```xaml\n<CollectionView \n    RemainingItemsThreshold=\"null\"\n    SelectionMode=\"Single\"\n    SelectionChanged=\"OnProdSelectionChanged\"\n    ItemsSource=\"{Binding ProdListS}\"\n    x:Name=\"prodcollect\">\n    <CollectionView.ItemsLayout>\n        <GridItemsLayout Orientation=\"Vertical\"\n                            Span=\"2\"/>\n    </CollectionView.ItemsLayout>\n</CollectionView>\n```\n\nOr, if you prefer to use the `RemainingItemsThresholdReachedCommand` binding:\n\n```xaml\n<CollectionView \n    RemainingItemsThresholdReachedCommand=\"{Binding LoadMoreS}\"\n    SelectionMode=\"Single\"\n    SelectionChanged=\"OnProdSelectionChanged\"\n    ItemsSource=\"{Binding ProdListS}\"\n    x:Name=\"prodcollect\">\n    <CollectionView.ItemsLayout>\n        <GridItemsLayout Orientation=\"Vertical\"\n                            Span=\"2\"/>\n    </CollectionView.ItemsLayout>\n</CollectionView>\n```"
