"```python\nimport os\nfrom PIL import Image\nfrom PyAV import AV\n\n# Define the file path and output file name\nfolderpath = \"output\"\nfilename = \"webp_image.webp\"\n\n# Get the encoder for webp\nmy_webp_encoder = AVEncoder()\n\n# Save the image as a webp file\nimage = Image.open(\"image.png\")\nimage.save(folderpath + \"/\" + filename, format=\"webp\", quality=90)\n\n# Define the encoder parameters\nquality = 90\nwidth = 640\nheight = 480\n\n# Create an encoder parameter object\nencoder_param = {\n    \"quality\": quality,\n    \"width\": width,\n    \"height\": height\n}\n\n# Create an encoder parameter object\nencoder = my_webp_encoder.get_encoder(\"image/webp\", encoder_param)\nencoder.set_quality(25)\nencoder.write(\"webp_image.webp\")\n```\n\nThis Python code saves an image as a webp file using the PyAV library, which provides an efficient way to encode audio and video files. The webp encoder is used here to save the image as a webp file. The `quality` parameter is set to 90 to reduce the quality of the image, which should help in reducing the file size."
