"```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef find_centroid(points):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the centroid of a polygon given its points.\n\n    Parameters:\n    points (numpy array): A 2D array of points, where each point is a tuple of two numbers.\n\n    Returns:\n    numpy array: The centroid of the polygon, represented as a tuple of two numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Ensure the input points are a numpy array\n    points = np.asarray(points)\n\n    # Calculate the mean of each row (x-coordinate)\n    centroid_x = np.mean(points, axis=1)\n\n    # Calculate the mean of each row (y-coordinate)\n    centroid_y = np.mean(points, axis=0)\n\n    return centroid_x, centroid_y\n\npoints = np.array([(0,0), (70,0), (70,25), (45,45), (45,180), (95,188), (95,200), (-25,200), (-25, 188), (25,180), (25,45), (0, 25), (0,0)])\ncentroid_x, centroid_y = find_centroid(points)\n\nprint(\"Centroid:\", (centroid_x, centroid_y))\n```"
