"You're getting a socket connection timeout error when trying to ping to Cloudinary. This error typically occurs when the connection to the Cloudinary server takes too long to establish.\n\n```python\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def ping_cloudinary():\n    try:\n        # Establish a connection to the Cloudinary server\n        cloudinary.api.ping()\n        return True\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error pinging Cloudinary: {e}\")\n        return False\n\nasync def upload_image(cover_image):\n    try:\n        # Ping the Cloudinary server to check the connection\n        if await ping_cloudinary():\n            # Upload the image to Cloudinary\n            cloudinary.uploader.upload(cover_image)\n            return True\n        else:\n            print(\"Cloudinary connection is not available\")\n            return False\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error uploading image: {e}\")\n        return False\n\nasync def add_product(req, res, next):\n    cover_image = req.body.get('coverImage')\n    image_array = req.body.get('imageArray')\n\n    # Check if cover_image and image_array are provided\n    if not cover_image or not image_array:\n        return res.status(400).json({\"error\": \"Cover image and image array are required.\"})\n\n    # Ping the Cloudinary server to check the connection\n    if await upload_image(cover_image):\n        # Upload the image to Cloudinary\n        if image_array:\n            for image in image_array:\n                await upload_image(image)\n            return res.status(200).json({\"message\": \"Images uploaded successfully.\"})\n        else:\n            return res.status(400).json({\"error\": \"At least one image is required.\"})\n    else:\n        return res.status(500).json({\"error\": \"Failed to upload images.\"})\n```\n\nThis code defines an asynchronous function `ping_cloudinary` that establishes a connection to the Cloudinary server and checks if the connection is available. If the connection is available, it uploads the image to Cloudinary.\n\nThe `add_product` function checks if the `cover_image` and `image_array` are provided and if the connection to Cloudinary is available. If the connection is available, it uploads the image to Cloudinary. If the connection is not available, it returns a 500 error with a message indicating that the connection is not available.\n\nNote that this code assumes that the `cover_image` and `image_array` are provided as part of the request body. You may need to modify the code to handle this differently depending on your specific use case."
"```python\nfrom databricks import dbutils\nfrom databricks import db\nfrom databricks.api.rest_api import get_rest_api\nfrom databricks.api.rest_api import PostRequest\nfrom databricks.api.rest_api import PostResponse\nfrom databricks.api.rest_api import PostError\nfrom databricks.api.rest_api import get_response\n\n# Create a REST API client\nrest_api = get_rest_api()\n\n# Define the endpoint and method\nendpoint = \"/apis/delta-tables/v1.0\"\nmethod = \"POST\"\n\n# Define the request body\nrequest_body = {\n    \"delta_table_name\": \"my_delta_table\",\n    \"delta_table_id\": \"my_delta_table_id\"\n}\n\n# Create the request\nrequest = PostRequest(\n    endpoint=endpoint,\n    method=method,\n    body=request_body\n)\n\n# Send the request\nresponse = rest_api.send_request(request)\n\n# Check if the request was successful\nif not response.status_code == 201:\n    raise PostError(\"Failed to create delta table\")\n\n# Get the response data\ndata = response.body\n\n# Print the response data\nprint(data)\n```\n\nPlease note that you need to have the necessary permissions and roles to create a REST API in Databricks. Also, this code assumes that you have already created a delta table in Databricks and have the necessary permissions to access it."
