"To render a functional component that is async in Jest, you can use the `useEffect` hook to handle the async operation and then render the component. Here's an example of how you can do it:\n\n```javascript\nimport React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';\n\nconst getParticipantsData = async () => {\n  // Simulate an async API call\n  const participantsData = await Promise.resolve({\n    participants: [\n      { id: 1, name: 'Participant 1' },\n      { id: 2, name: 'Participant 2' },\n    ],\n  });\n\n  return participantsData;\n};\n\nconst ParticipantsTable = ({ participantsData }) => {\n  const [participants, setParticipants] = useState(participantsData);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    getParticipantsData();\n  }, []);\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Participants Table</h1>\n      <table>\n        <thead>\n          <tr>\n            <th>ID</th>\n            <th>Name</th>\n          </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n          {participants.map((participant) => (\n            <tr key={participant.id}>\n              <td>{participant.id}</td>\n              <td>{participant.name}</td>\n            </tr>\n          ))}\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default ParticipantsTable;\n```\n\nIn this example, we use the `useEffect` hook to call `getParticipantsData` when the component mounts. We then use the `useState` hook to store the result of the API call in the `participantsData` state variable.\n\nYou can then render the `ParticipantsTable` component inside the `Home` component, like this:\n\n```javascript\nimport React from 'react';\nimport ParticipantsTable from './ParticipantsTable';\n\nconst Home = () => {\n  const participantsData = getParticipantsData();\n\n  return (\n    <div data-testid=\"home-page\">\n      <ParticipantsTable participantsData={participantsData} />\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default Home;\n```\n\nThis way, the `ParticipantsTable` component will be rendered only when the `Home` component mounts, and it will be an instance of the `ParticipantsTable` component with the actual data."
