"Here's how you can create a test file for the update function in Elm.\n\n```python\nimport os\nimport json\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, TypeVar, Union\n\nT = TypeVar('T')\n\nclass File:\n    def __init__(self, name: str, content: bytes):\n        self.name = name\n        self.content = content\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return f\"File(name='{self.name}', content={self.content})\"\n\n\nclass FileInfo:\n    def __init__(self, name: str, content: bytes):\n        self.name = name\n        self.content = content\n\n    def __str__(self):\n        return f\"FileInfo(name='{self.name}', content={self.content})\"\n\n\ndef create_file(name: str, content: bytes) -> File:\n    return File(name, content)\n\n\ndef create_file_upload_info_list() -> List[FileInfo]:\n    return [FileInfo(\"test1\", create_file(\"test1\", b\"test1 content\"))]\n\n\ndef create_modal_selected_file() -> FileInfo:\n    return FileInfo(\"test2\", create_file(\"test2\", b\"test2 content\"))\n\n\ndef create_modal_file_upload_info_list() -> List[FileInfo]:\n    return [FileInfo(\"test3\", create_file(\"test3\", b\"test3 content\"))]\n\n\ndef create_file_fuzzer() -> List[File]:\n    return [\n        create_file(\"test1\", b\"test1 content\"),\n        create_file(\"test2\", b\"test2 content\"),\n        create_file(\"test3\", b\"test3 content\"),\n        create_file_upload_info_list(),\n        create_modal_selected_file(),\n        create_modal_file_upload_info_list(),\n    ]\n\n\ndef create_file_fuzzer_file(file: Optional[File]) -> None:\n    if file:\n        print(json.dumps(file.__dict__, indent=4))\n    else:\n        print(\"No file provided\")\n\n\n# Usage\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    file_fuzzer = create_file_fuzzer()\n\n    for file in file_fuzzer:\n        create_file_fuzzer_file(file)\n```\n\nIn this code, we have created a `File` class to represent files, and a `FileInfo` class to represent file information. We have also created a list of `File` instances and `FileInfo` instances to represent different types of files. The `create_file_fuzzer` function generates these files and prints their contents to the console.\n\nWe have also created a list of `File` instances and `FileInfo` instances to represent different types of files, and a function to create a list of files.\n\nFinally, we have created a function `create_file_fuzzer_file` that takes a file instance or None and prints its contents to the console."
