"```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef find_n_closest_points(data, target_point, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the n closest points to a given target point in a list of points.\n\n    Args:\n    - data (list): A list of [longitude, latitude] arrays.\n    - target_point (tuple): The target point [longitude, latitude].\n    - n (int): The number of closest points to find.\n\n    Returns:\n    - closest_points (list): A list of the n closest points.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Convert the data to a NumPy array for efficient calculations\n    data = np.array(data)\n\n    # Calculate the Euclidean distance from the target point to each point in the data\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(data - target_point, axis=1)\n\n    # Combine the distances with their indices\n    distances_with_indices = np.hstack((distances, np.arange(len(data))))\n\n    # Sort the distances with their indices\n    sorted_indices = np.sort(distances_with_indices)[:n]\n\n    # Get the indices of the n smallest distances\n    indices = sorted_indices[:n]\n\n    # Extract the n closest points from the data\n    closest_points = data[indices]\n\n    return closest_points\n\n# Example usage:\ndata = [\n    [103.6632, 1.32287],\n    [103.66506, 1.30803],\n    [103.67088, 1.32891],\n    [103.67636, 1.3354],\n    [103.67669, 1.32779],\n    [103.67927, 1.31477],\n    [103.67927, 1.32757],\n    [103.67958, 1.31458],\n    [103.68508, 1.32469],\n    [103.6927, 1.3386],\n    [103.69367, 1.34],\n    [103.69377, 1.37058],\n    [103.69431, 1.37161],\n    [103.69519, 1.35543],\n    [103.69538, 1.34725],\n    [103.6961, 1.33667],\n    [103.696918716667, 1.35110788333333],\n    [103.69731, 1.35],\n    [103.698615333333, 1.33590666666667],\n    [103.69975, 1.35],\n    [103.70129, 1.34],\n    [103.70247, 1.34],\n    [103.70366, 1.34],\n    [103.70394, 1.33948],\n    [103.70403, 1.34081],\n    [103.704697166667, 1.33546383333333],\n    [103.70504, 1.34],\n    [103.706281333333, 1.344646],\n    [103.70689, 1.34464]\n]\n\ntarget_point = (103.6632, 1.32287)\nn = 3\n\nclosest_points = find_n_closest_points(data, target_point, n)\n\nprint(closest_points)\n```\n\nThis code uses NumPy to efficiently calculate the Euclidean distances from the target point to each point in the data, and then sorts the distances with their indices. It then extracts the n smallest distances and returns the corresponding points. The example usage demonstrates how to use this function with a sample dataset and target point."
"```python\ndef sort_array(arr):\n    # Create a dictionary to store the children of each block\n    children_dict = {}\n    for item in arr:\n        if item['id'] not in children_dict:\n            children_dict[item['id']] = []\n        children_dict[item['id']].append(item)\n\n    # Function to find the parent of an item\n    def find_parent(item):\n        for parent in arr:\n            if parent['id'] == item['parentId']:\n                return parent\n        return None\n\n    # Function to get the children of a parent\n    def get_children(parent):\n        return children_dict.get(parent['id'], [])\n\n    # Function to sort an item\n    def sort_item(item):\n        parent = find_parent(item)\n        if parent:\n            # If the item has children, sort them first\n            if parent['children']:\n                parent['children'] = [sort_item(child) for child in parent['children']]\n            # Then sort the item itself\n            item['children'] = sorted(item['children'], key=lambda child: child['id'])\n        return item\n\n    # Sort the array\n    for item in arr:\n        item = sort_item(item)\n\n    return arr\n\narr = [\n    {id: 3123124, parentId: 0o0000, title: 'title', type: 'block'},\n    {id: 3542132, parentId: 3123124, title: 'title', type: 'child'},\n    {id: 54232, parentId: 3123124, title: 'title', type: 'child'},\n    {id: 986648, parentId: 3123124, title: 'title', type: 'block'},\n    {id: 45324, parentId: 0o0000, title: 'title', type: 'block'},\n    {id: 99999, parentId: 45324, title: 'title', type: 'child'},\n    {id: 88888, parentId: 45324, title: 'title', type: 'block'},\n    {id: 77777, parentId: 88888, title: 'title', type: 'child'},\n    {id: 12345, parentId: 88888, title: 'title', type: 'block'},\n    {id: 56445, parentId: 12345, title: 'title', type: 'child'},\n    {id: 24124, parentId: 12345, title: 'title', type: 'child'},\n    {id: 15075, parentId: 12345, title: 'title', type: 'block'},\n    {id: 54308, parentId: 15075, title: 'title', type: 'child'},\n    {id: 66666, parentId: 88888, title: 'title', type: 'block'},\n    {id: 84356, parentId: 66666, title: 'title', type: 'child'},\n]\nnewArr = sort_array(arr)\n\nfor item in newArr:\n    print(item)\n```"
