"```python\nimport SwiftUI\n\nstruct DatePickerView: View {\n    @State private var isFieldEditing = false\n    @State private var datePicker: Date = Date()\n    @State private var isDatePickerOpen = false\n\n    var body: some View {\n        VStack {\n            if isDatePickerOpen {\n                Text(\"Date: \\(String(format: \"%d-%m-%Y\", datePicker))\")\n                    .padding(.bottom)\n            } else {\n                Text(\"Date: \\(String(format: \"%d-%m-%Y\", datePicker))\")\n                    .padding(.bottom, 16)\n            }\n            .onTapGesture {\n                isDatePickerOpen = true\n                isFieldEditing = false\n                datePicker = Date()\n            }\n            .sheet(isPresented: $isDatePickerOpen) {\n                DatePicker(selection: $datePicker, displayedComponents: .date)\n                    .labelsHidden()\n                    .padding(.trailing, 8)\n                    .frame(alignment: .leading)\n                    .colorMultiply(AppColors.textNavy100Color)\n                    .accentColor(AppColors.textNavy100Color)\n                    .onTapGesture {\n                        isDatePickerOpen = false\n                        isFieldEditing = true\n                        isDatePickerOpen = true\n                        datePicker = Date()\n                    }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nstruct DatePickerView_Previews: PreviewProvider {\n    static var previews: some View {\n        DatePickerView()\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis code creates a `DatePickerView` that displays a date picker in a SwiftUI view. When the user taps on the date picker, it opens up and displays a calendar. When the user taps somewhere else on the screen, the date picker closes and its parent view's border color changes to `AppColors.textNavy100Color`. The code also includes a `@State` variable to track whether the date picker is open and whether the user is editing the date. The date picker's border color is set when the user taps on it, and it is set to `AppColors.textNavy100Color` when the date picker is closed."
"```kotlin\nfun periodBetween(date1: String, date2: String): String {\n    val pattern = \"P*(\\\\d{4})*(Y|M|D)\"\n    val matches = date1.matchAll(pattern)\n    val years = matches[1].joinToString(\" \")\n    val months = matches[2].joinToString(\" \")\n    val days = matches[3].joinToString(\" \")\n\n    return \"$years$months$days\"\n}\n\nfun main() {\n    val date1 = \"2022-01-01\"\n    val date2 = \"2022-12-31\"\n    println(periodBetween(date1, date2))\n}\n```\n\nIn this code, we use regular expressions to extract the year, month, and day from the input string. The pattern `P*(\\\\d{4})*(Y|M|D)` matches one or more digits followed by either `Y`, `M`, or `D`. The `joinToString` function is used to concatenate the matches into a single string."
