"None\n\nYou are trying to use `useSession` and `SessionProvider` from `next-auth/react` in your `layout.tsx` file, but the `useSession` hook must be wrapped in a `SessionProvider` component. \n\nHere is how you can modify your `layout.tsx` file to fix the issue:\n\n```typescript\nimport { SessionProvider } from 'next-auth/react';\nimport { ReactNode } from 'react';\nimport React from 'react';\n\nimport 'globals.css';\nimport Link from 'next/link';\n\ntype Props = {\n  children: ReactNode;\n  session: any;\n};\n\nexport default function Layout({ children, session }: Props) {\n  return (\n    <SessionProvider session={session}>\n      <html lang=\"en\">\n        <head />\n        <body>\n          <div className=\"mx-auto\">\n            <div className=\"flex flex-row flex-wrap\">\n              <aside className=\"w-full sm:w-1/3 md:w-1/5 xl:w-1/6 border-r-2 border-[#F845C6]\" />\n              <div className=\"w-full sm:w-2/3 md:w-4/5 xl:w-5/6\">\n                {children}\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </body>\n      </html>\n    </SessionProvider>\n  );\n}\n\nexport function getLayout(page: any) {\n  const { session } = page.props;\n\n  return (\n    <SessionProvider session={session}>\n      <Layout session={session}>{page}</Layout>\n    </SessionProvider>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nAnd in your `login.tsx` file:\n\n```typescript\nimport { getLayout } from '../components/Layout';\n\nexport default function Login() {\n  const { data: session } = useSession();\n  console.log(session);\n\n  if (session) {\n    return (\n      <div style={{ fontFamily: 'sans-serif', margin: '10px 20px' }} />\n    );\n  } else {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <p>Please sign in</p>\n        <button onClick={() => signIn('google', { callbackUrl: '/account' })}>\n          Sign in with Google\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    );\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis should resolve the error you are seeing."
