"The `ProviderSettings` class is not available in the provided package. You need to add the following dependency to your `pom.xml` file:\n\n```xml\n<dependency>\n    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-security</artifactId>\n</dependency>\n```\n\nYou also need to add the following dependency to your `pom.xml` file:\n\n```xml\n<dependency>\n    <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>\n    <artifactId>spring-security-oauth2-authorization-server</artifactId>\n    <version>1.0.1</version>\n</dependency>\n```\n\nHowever, you don't need to manually create a `ProviderSettings` class. You can simply import the `ProviderSettings` class from the `spring-security-oauth2-authorization-server` package:\n\n```java\nimport org.springframework.security.oauth2.server.authrization.config.ProviderSettings;\n```\n\nThis should resolve the issue."
