"```\nfrom shapely import wkt\n\ndef test_max_count_constraint():\n    # Define the property and its path\n    property_path = \"http://example.org/shacl#valueIfExists\"\n\n    # Define the shape with the path to the attribute\n    shape_path = \"http://example.org/shacl#ex:shape\"\n\n    # Define the constraint component\n    constraint = {\n        \"type\": \"MaxCount\",\n        \"maxCount\": 1,\n        \"minCount\": 0,\n    }\n\n    # Define the test data\n    test_data = [\n        {\"ex:TestClass\": \"Test_OK_nothing\"},\n        {\"ex:TestClass\": \"Test_OK_1\"},\n        {\"ex:TestClass\": \"Test_OK_1_2\"},\n        {\"ex:TestClass\": \"Test_Not_OK\"},\n    ]\n\n    # Create a valid shape\n    valid_shape = wkt.loads(\"http://example.org/shacl#ex:shape\")  # Replace with a valid shape\n\n    # Apply the constraint to the shape\n    validated_shape = wkt.loads(f\"({shape_path}: {valid_shape})\")  # Replace with the path to the attribute\n\n    # Apply the constraint component to the validated shape\n    validated_shape = validated_shape.apply(constraint)\n\n    # Apply the constraint component to the test data\n    for test_case in test_data:\n        if test_case[\"ex:TestClass\"] == \"Test_OK_1_2\":\n            test_case[\"ex:valueIfExists\"] = [\"ok\", \"other 1\", \"other 2\"]\n        elif test_case[\"ex:TestClass\"] == \"Test_Not_OK\":\n            test_case[\"ex:valueIfExists\"] = [\"other 1\", \"other 2\"]\n\n    # Validate the test data\n    for test_case in test_data:\n        validated_test_case = validated_shape.apply(test_case)\n        if not validated_test_case:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n\nprint(test_max_count_constraint())\n```"
"To prevent the \"View Saved Logins\" message from covering up the \"Please enter an email address\" message, you can add the following code to your HTML form:\n\n```html\n<p>I have a simple HTML form, something like:</p>\n<pre class=\"lang-html prettyprint-override\"><code>&lt;form action = &quot;register.php&quot; method = &quot;post&quot; autocomplete = &quot;off&quot;&gt; \n    &lt;input type = &quot;email&quot; name = &quot;email&quot; placeholder = &quot;Email&quot; id = &quot;email&quot; required&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; value=&quot;Register&quot;&gt;    \n    &lt;input type=&quot;hidden&quot; name=&quot;hidden&quot; value=&quot;email&quot; /&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<p>By setting <code>type = &quot;email&quot;</code>, some helpful validation features are activated. For example if I enter an &quot;email&quot; that does not have the @ symbol and try to submit the form, a message &quot;Please enter an email address&quot; will appear. Unfortunately, in my browser (Firefox), this helpful message is covered up by a &quot;View Saved Logins&quot; message. To prevent this, we can add a hidden input field that will override the &quot;View Saved Logins&quot; message. The hidden input field should have the same name as the email input field and should be set to a value of an empty string. This will cause the browser to display the &quot;View Saved Logins&quot; message instead of the email input field.</p>\n<pre class=\"lang-html prettyprint-override\"><code>&lt;form action = &quot;register.php&quot; method = &quot;post&quot; autocomplete = &quot;off&quot;&gt; \n    &lt;input type = &quot;email&quot; name = &quot;email&quot; placeholder = &quot;Email&quot; id = &quot;email&quot; required&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; value=&quot;Register&quot;&gt;    \n    &lt;input type=&quot;hidden&quot; name=&quot;hidden&quot; value=&quot;&quot; /&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;\n</code></pre>\n```\n\nIn this code, the hidden input field with the name \"hidden\" and value \"\" will override the \"View Saved Logins\" message. The \"View Saved Logins\" message will be displayed only when the email input field is empty."
