"None\nYou can get the host and port of the UDP server using the `gethostbyname` function from the `Net::IP::Addr` module.\n\n```python\nuse Net::IP::Addr;\n\nmy $socket = IO::Socket::Async.bind-udp: 'localhost', 3333;\n\nreact whenever $socket.Supply: :bin {\n    say \"Received some junk: { .gist }&quot;;    \n}\n\ngiven IO::Socket::Async.udp {\n    await .print-to: 'localhost', 3333, 'Hello';\n}\n\nmy $host = $socket.gethostbyname('localhost');\nmy $port = $socket.getpeername(3333)[2];\n```\n\nOr, you can use the `getaddrinfo` function to get the host and port from the address information of the incoming connection.\n\n```python\nuse Net::IP::Addr;\n\nmy $socket = IO::Socket::Async.bind-udp: 'localhost', 3333;\n\nreact whenever $socket.Supply: :bin {\n    say \"Received some junk: { .gist }&quot;;    \n}\n\ngiven IO::Socket::Async.udp {\n    await .print-to: 'localhost', 3333, 'Hello';\n}\n\nmy $host = $socket.getaddrinfo('localhost', 3333)[0].host;\nmy $port = $socket.getaddrinfo('localhost', 3333)[0].port;\n```"
