"```python\nclass Eeg:\n    def __init__(self, data):\n        self.data = data\n\nclass Analysis(S4::ClassOf):\n    S4_TYPE = \"Analysis\"\n\n    def __init__(self, eeg):\n        self.eeg = eeg\n        self.eeg_copy = eeg.copy()  # Store a constant reference to the original eeg object\n\n    @method\n    def perform_analysis(self):\n        return self.eeg_copy.data  # Access the original eeg data without duplication\n\n    @method\n    def manipulate_eeg(self, new_data):\n        self.eeg.data = new_data  # Update the original eeg data without duplication\n        self.eeg_copy.data = new_data  # Update the copy of the original eeg data\n\n    @method\n    def copy_eeg(self):\n        return self.eeg_copy  # Create a copy of the original eeg object\n\n# Example usage:\neeg_data = [1, 2, 3]\nanalysis = Analysis(Eeg(eeg_data))\nprint(analysis.perform_analysis())  # Output: [1, 2, 3]\nanalysis.manipulate_eeg([4, 5, 6])\nprint(eeg_data)  # Output: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\nanalysis.copy_eeg()\nprint(eeg_data)  # Output: [1, 2, 3]\n```"
