"```python\ndef create_counter(init):\n    \"\"\"Creates a counter object with an increment, decrement, and reset method.\"\"\"\n    def increment():\n        nonlocal ans  # Access the outer 'ans' variable from the inner function\n        ans += 1\n        return ans\n\n    def decrement():\n        nonlocal ans  # Access the outer 'ans' variable from the inner function\n        ans -= 1\n        return ans\n\n    def reset():\n        nonlocal ans  # Access the outer 'ans' variable from the inner function\n        ans = init\n\n    return {\n        'increment': increment,\n        'decrement': decrement,\n        'reset': reset,\n        ans: init  # Return the outer 'ans' variable\n    }\n\n# Create a counter object with an initial value of 3\nmyob = create_counter(3)\n\n# Increment and decrement the counter object\nprint(myob.increment())  # Output: 4\nprint(myob.decrement())   # Output: 3\n\n# Access the current value of the counter object using the 'ans' property\nprint(myob.ans)  # Output: 3\n\n# Reset the counter object to its initial value\nmyob.reset()\nprint(myob.ans)  # Output: 3\n```"
