"extern int **foo;  // extern variable prototype: comparison of array not equal to a null pointer is always true.\n\nThe issue is due to the way the compiler handles arrays and pointers in C. When you declare an array, it allocates memory for all elements in the array. However, when you declare a pointer to an array, it only points to the first element of the array. \n\nIn your case, `foo` is an array of integers, but you're trying to pass it as a pointer to another array. This is why GCC is warning you about the relocation against `foo` in a read-only section.\n\nTo fix this, you should use `*foo` instead of `foo` when passing the array to another function. \n\nHere's the corrected code:\n\n```c\nextern int **foo;\n\nint main() {\n    if (*foo != NULL)  // Use *\n    {\n        printf(\"Foo is not null\\n\");\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n```"
"```python\nimport sys\nfrom PySide2.QtWidgets import QApplication, QWidget, QVBoxLayout, QPushButton, QFileDialog, QFileDialogButton, QLabel, QStackedLayout\nfrom PySide2.QtGui import QPixmap\n\nclass Application(QWidget):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n\n        self.image_pics = [None, None, None, None]\n\n        self.layout = QVBoxLayout()\n\n        self.button_stack = QStackedLayout()\n\n        self.button_stack.addWidget(QPushButton(\"Button A\"))\n        self.button_stack.addWidget(QPushButton(\"Button B\"))\n        self.button_stack.addWidget(QPushButton(\"Button C\"))\n        self.button_stack.addWidget(QPushButton(\"Button D\"))\n\n        self.button_stack.addWidget(QPushButton(\"BtnAll\"))\n        self.button_stack.addWidget(QPushButton(\"BtnA\"))\n        self.button_stack.addWidget(QPushButton(\"BtnB\"))\n        self.button_stack.addWidget(QPushButton(\"BtnC\"))\n        self.button_stack.addWidget(QPushButton(\"BtnD\"))\n\n        self.layout.addWidget(QLabel(\"Image 1\"))\n        self.layout.addWidget(QLabel(\"Image 2\"))\n        self.layout.addWidget(QLabel(\"Image 3\"))\n        self.layout.addWidget(QLabel(\"Image 4\"))\n        self.layout.addWidget(QLabel(\"Image 5\"))\n\n        self.setLayout(self.layout)\n\n        self.load_button = QPushButton(\"Load\")\n        self.load_button.clicked.connect(self.load_images)\n\n        self.button_stack.addWidget(self.load_button)\n\n        self.load_button.clicked.connect(self.stack_images)\n\n    def load_images(self):\n        file_name, _ = QFileDialog.getOpenFileName(self, \"Open File\", \"\", \"Image Files (*.png *.jpg *.jpeg *.bmp)\")\n        if file_name:\n            self.image_pics = [QPixmap(file_name), QPixmap(file_name), QPixmap(file_name), QPixmap(file_name), QPixmap(file_name)]\n\n    def stack_images(self):\n        for i in range(len(self.image_pics)):\n            if self.image_pics[i]:\n                if i < len(self.image_pics) - 1:\n                    self.image_pics[i].setScaledContents(True)\n                    self.image_pics[i].scaled(400, 400, Qt.KeepAspectRatio)\n                else:\n                    self.image_pics[i].setScaledContents(True)\n                    self.image_pics[i].scaled(400, 400, Qt.KeepAspectRatio)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    app = QApplication(sys.argv)\n    ex = Application()\n    ex.show()\n    sys.exit(app.exec_())\n```"
