"**Fine-Grained Personal Access Token Permissions**\n\nWhen creating a fine-grained personal access token, you should choose the following permissions:\n\n* `repo`: Allows access to the repository, including its contents and history.\n* `push`: Allows pushing changes to the repository.\n* `pull`: Allows pulling changes from the repository.\n* `read:org`: Allows viewing information about the organization, including its members and repositories.\n* `read:private repositories`: Allows viewing information about private repositories.\n\nThese permissions will allow you to push and pull changes to your repository, but you should not select `repo` permission if you don't know what it means. The `repo` permission is required to access the repository, but it's not necessary to access the contents of the repository.\n\n**Fine-Grained Personal Access Token Selection**\n\nWhen creating a fine-grained personal access token, you should select the following permissions:\n\n* `repo`\n* `push`\n* `pull`\n* `read:org`\n* `read:private repositories`"
