"You can use the `github.actions/skip-workflow-run` action to skip a workflow run without disabling the entire workflow. This action allows you to specify a workflow run ID or name to skip, and it will skip the entire workflow without affecting the version control history.\n\nHere's an example of how you can use this action in your workflow:\n\n```yml\nname: CICD\n\n# ...\n\njobs:\n  CI:\n    uses: actions/skip-workflow-run@v1\n    with:\n      workflowRunId: 'your-workflow-run-id'\n      workflowRunName: 'your-workflow-run-name'\n```\n\nThis will skip the specified workflow run without disabling the entire workflow. Note that you need to use the `actions/skip-workflow-run` action version `v1` to use this feature."
